{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"Switch an automation on"},"description":"Switches one automation on, running the version named (version_id), older or newer, got ready first if it never was; left out, the newest, which deploy_automation gets ready first. A version with a step that has to be confirmed by name is got ready with deploy_automation and confirm_actions first. From then on it acts on its own whenever what it starts on happens, and its steps run as they are built, which can include WhatsApp messages to customers. A recipe set up with a second automation switches on with it. actions names every action the version\u2019s steps take, and the second automation\u2019s, from the list in the schema (an automation\u2019s versions list theirs as actions); a list that leaves one out or names another is refused, with the right list. The preview refuses that list as the call would, and gives no token. Each call needs confirming: without confirmation_token it changes nothing and returns a preview and a token for a person to approve; called again with that token, it switches it on.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"actions":{"description":"Every action the automation\u2019s steps take, and those of a second automation set up with it, each once: what a person approves it doing. A list that leaves one out, or names one the steps do not take, is refused, and the refusal gives the list in `error.actions`. A version\u2019s `actions` lists them too.","items":{"enum":["integration.call","whatsapp.send_text","whatsapp.send_template","whatsapp.send_media","whatsapp.send_interactive","whatsapp.mark_read","whatsapp.typing_on","whatsapp.send_list","whatsapp.send_location","whatsapp.send_catalogue","contact.upsert","contact.tag","contact.untag","contact.set_field","contact.get","contacts.query","contact.set_opt_out","contact.merge","conversation.get","conversation.handoff","conver